{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012fW2tHj5urjj9hdbmrktdx","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"The proposal is that brokers and observer controllers can start without having previously run `kafka-storage format`, and when the `--cluster-id` flag is supplied the `meta.properties` file will be written with **version 2**.  \\\\n\\\\n- 2026-01-06T13:18:38.000000Z - `mail:8e958fd66bd3b2546376c7fe`: Kevin Wu opens the discussion on KIP-1262, stating the goal is to remove the need to run `kafka-storage format` before starting brokers and observer controllers.  \\\\n- 2026-02-25T20:57:18.000000Z - `mail:fc43d61fdfdfa544476d4f34`: Alyssa Huang notes that “meta.properties V2 will be written on newly formatted nodes + non-formatting nodes” and that starting Kafka on any node requires `cluster.id` to be present in `meta.properties`.  \\\\n- 2026-02-25T22:22:53.000000Z - `mail:7e3fc0f2797ee6e2a63766ef`: Kevin Wu confirms that “meta.properties V2 will be written on newly formatted nodes + non-formatting nodes” and that the node must have `cluster.id` in `meta.properties` when starting.  \\\\n- 2026-02-26T18:36:08.000000Z - `mail:114ea15d5f65819265676872`: Alyssa Huang reiterates that “meta.properties V2 will be written on newly formatted nodes + non-formatting nodes” and that the presence of `cluster.id` is required for startup.  \\\\n\\\\nNo record contradicts this instant; earlier messages only propose the change, and later messages confirm the decision.  \\\\n\\\\nNothing could be determined about a formal KIP approval or implementation commit.\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"mail:114ea15d5f65819265676872\\\",\\\"mail:7e3fc0f2797ee6e2a63766ef\\\",\\\"mail:8e958fd66bd3b2546376c7fe\\\",\\\"mail:fc43d61fdfdfa544476d4f34\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":111.604,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":22,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":null,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":null,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.00416959,\\\"inpu